    "result_text": "The full suite runs the acceptance tests (the only tests in this project) \u2014 all green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule: **SILVER** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **BRONZE**.\n\nSince `membershipTier` is a derived, read-only response field (like the existing `displayName`/`initials`), I followed the same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing the tier:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n\nThe tier is computed at read time, so it applies to both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`. `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
